REQUIREMENTS
------------

- a shell environment
- VMD
- PROPKA
- Python with standard scientific packages (numpy, matplotlib)


HOW TO RUN
----------

1. Download PDB file 6kgx-assembly1.cif from PDB databank
2. Enter folder 1_selections, open VMD and execute the script extractor_chain.tcl
   This will create PDB files for every chain in the large protein assembly 6kgx along with adjacent chains
3. Enter in folder 2_pka and execute launch.sh.
   This will call PROPKA on each previously extracted atomic structure
4. Enter in folder 3_sasa, open VMD and call extract_sasa.tcl.
   This will calculate the SASA of all lysine side chains.
5. Enter in folder 4_aggregate and call aggregate_data.py.
   This will aggregate data gathered in folders 2_pka and 3_sasa, using information from file chains_summary.dat (manually created from PDB databank data).
